00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:07.380
SPEAKER 1: Hello, everyone.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.730
My name is Juan [INAUDIBLE],,
and I am a product manager

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.100
in the continuous integration,
continuous delivery

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.960
team in Google Cloud.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.230
Today I am going to
tell you about Artifact

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:20.960
Registry, the evolution of
Google Container Registry.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.450
As the evolution of
Google Container Registry,

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:25.790
Artifact Registry
includes new features

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.850
like regional repositories,
multiple repositories

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:32.570
per project, and repository
native identity access

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:33.540
management.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:36.170
Artifact Registry
gives you a scalable

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:39.710
build artifact management
with security and control.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:42.830
You can focus on differentiating
your product offering

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:46.580
while enjoying the peace of mind
of knowing that your software

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:50.270
delivery process is backed
by Google Cloud Platform.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.340
Artifact Registry
is currently in beta

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:55.820
with Docker support and
alpha support for Java

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.740
and node.js artifacts.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.110
Now my teammate
Ray will show you

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:03.590
how Artifact Registry integrates
into the Java development

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:05.830
and release process.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:09.450
RAY: Here we have a
simple Java microservice.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:13.620
As you can see, we have created
different artifact repositories

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.460
in this GCP project to
manage the build artifacts

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.110
for this application--

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.450
one for container
images and another

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.940
for Java Maven artifacts.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:28.530
These repositories are located
in specific GCP regions,

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:32.760
and they are configured with a
new repository native identity

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:36.430
access management provided
by Artifact Registry.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:38.790
For example, permissions
are configured

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:43.540
to control who can
push or pull artifacts.

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:45.520
Artifact Registry
easily integrates

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:48.490
with your development
and release tool set.

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:51.160
If you are building a
common library in Java

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:53.890
to be used by all of your
business applications,

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:57.760
you can use Maven or Grado to
build and publish the packages

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:01.070
to Artifact Registry.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:04.730
When building a container using
Docker or [INAUDIBLE] plug-in,

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:08.300
they can be configured to push
container images to Artifact

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.470
Registry as well.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:16.200
Now, with all the artifacts
stored in Artifact Registry,

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.830
you can manage those
packages via the console

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:21.080
and [INAUDIBLE] command
line while applying

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:24.620
consistent permissions
across your repositories.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.880
Artifact Registry
integrates with Cloud Build,

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:29.480
a third party CI/CD system.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.460
Here we have set up a
Cloud Build pipeline that

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:35.390
builds the application,
publishes the Maven artifact

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:38.270
the artifact registry,
then builds and stores

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:43.020
the container image in
Artifact Registry as well.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.590
From there, we can easily
deploy the container

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:50.210
into Google Cloud Runtimes such
as Kubernetes engine or Cloud

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:51.900
Run.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.810
Artifact Registry is the
evolution of Container Registry

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:58.490
and gives you scalable
build artifact management

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.530
with security and control.

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:02.720
Visit our documentation
to learn how

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:06.700
to get started with
Docker, Maven, and NPM

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.030
in Artifact Registry.

